    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.indentscope\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen I try to assign `animation = require('mini.indentscope').gen_animation.none()` I get the following error:\r\n```\r\nattempt to index field 'gen_animation' (a function value)\r\n```\r\nI fixed this issue by using `require('mini.indentscope').gen_animation('none')` but the documentation specifies to use `require('mini.indentscope').gen_animation.none()` for no animation.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.8.2\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n--- minimal.lua\r\nlocal indentscope = require('mini.indentscope')\r\nindentscope.setup({\r\n    draw = {\r\n        animation = indentscope.gen_animation.none()\r\n    }\r\n})\r\n```\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n`require('mini.indentscope').gen_animation.none()` should not throw an error and return a function that always return 0.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n`require('mini.indentscope').gen_animation.none()` throws the following error:\r\n```\r\nattempt to index field 'gen_animation' (a function value)\r\n```",
